infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Start empty and add vs start full and subtract
  desc Same lean image — but only one removes the attack surface by category, not by deletion
  compares
    - label Multi-stage build then COPY into scratch
      children
        - label Start empty: scratch plus COPY one binary
          desc Build tools never enter the final image — only the compiled artifact does
        - label Cannot be incomplete
          desc Start-empty-and-add has no removal step that can miss transitive files
        - label No shell, no package manager, no curl
          desc Nothing to weaponize after RCE — defense by absence
        - label OS-package scan finds nothing
          desc Zero OS packages, so the OS-layer scan is clean by construction
    - label debian then apt-get remove
      children
        - label Start full: debian, then apt-get remove
          desc Subtracts from a populated base image of ~200 packages
        - label Removal can miss transitive files
          desc Deletion is error-prone and often leaves dependencies behind
        - label Usually leaves a shell behind
          desc busybox/sh survives as a universal second stage
        - label Long CVE list, mostly noise
          desc ~200 packages flagged, many the Go binary never invokes
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
